Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: wire RTL8261x LED callbacks for RTL8261BE

The rtl8261x LED support merged in this tree (VEND2 LCR block at
0xd032/0xd040/0xd044, four LEDs with 5G/10G speed bits) is only wired
to the RTL8261C/RTL8261CE driver entries.  The RTL8261BE entry added
by 742-net-phy-realtek-add-5G-and-10G-PHY-support.patch matches the
same silicon family (per upstream notes, RTL8261N/BE share the RTL8261C
architecture) but ships no led_* callbacks, so of_phy_leds() ignores
any DT leds node ("no PHY driver support") and the 10G port LEDs stay
firmware-owned and invisible to the LED subsystem.

Wire the five existing rtl8261x_led_* callbacks into the BE entry.
This is the same hardware that upstream tests on a Gemtek W1700K
(Airoha AN7581) where LED index 2 is the amber and index 3 the green
LED of each 10G port; the XR1710G uses the same RTL8261BE on mdio 5.
With DT nodes added, netdev triggers offload to the PHY and no CPU
cycles are spent blinking.

No behavioural change for boards without a DT leds node under the
RTL8261BE PHY: phylib only registers LED class devices when one is
present.

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -4437,6 +4437,11 @@
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.led_brightness_set  = rtl8261x_led_brightness_set,
+		.led_hw_is_supported = rtl8261x_led_hw_is_supported,
+		.led_hw_control_get  = rtl8261x_led_hw_control_get,
+		.led_hw_control_set  = rtl8261x_led_hw_control_set,
+		.led_polarity_set    = rtl8261x_led_polarity_set,
 	}, {
 		.name           = "RTL8261N 10Gbps PHY",
 		.config_init    = rtl826x_config_init,
